        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Why an electric machine fits the traction requirement:\n\n  requirement            engine            motor\n  ------------------------------------------------\n  torque at 0 speed      NONE (clutch)     FULL\n  constant power range   narrow (6 gears)  wide (1 gear)\n  braking energy         lost as heat      RECOVERED\n  part-load efficiency   small island      broad plateau\n\nConsequence: the EV advantage is LARGEST in urban\ndriving (low speed, part load, frequent stops) and\nSMALLEST at steady high speed, where drag dominates\nand both vehicles simply push air.\n\nThe remaining four modules are therefore about HOW to\ncontrol motors, not WHETHER to use them.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.2, pp.33-44.' },
