        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Gear ratio selection is squeezed from BOTH ends:\n\n  LOW SPEED requirement (gradeability, acceleration):\n    i >= F_required * r_wheel / (T_motor * eta)\n    -> sets a MINIMUM ratio\n\n  TOP SPEED requirement:\n    i <= omega_motor_max * r_wheel / V_max\n    -> sets a MAXIMUM ratio\n\n  single gear works IF  i_min <= i_max\n\nThe WIDTH of that window is set entirely by the\nmachine SPEED RATIO. A narrow speed ratio can close\nthe window completely, forcing a second gear.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.4, pp.104-105.' },
