        terms: ['surplus effort', 'gradeability curve', 'acceleration profile', 'two phases', 'constant power phase'],
        definition:
          'Gradeability and acceleration both follow from the surplus tractive effort, which is now shaped by the motor characteristic. Below the speed corresponding to base speed the tractive effort is constant, so the acceleration is nearly constant and falls only as drag builds. Above it the effort falls hyperbolically and the acceleration declines rapidly. This gives the characteristic two-phase acceleration profile of an electric vehicle: strong and nearly constant acceleration up to a corner speed, then a progressively softening response.',
        takeaway: 'Constant torque gives a flat acceleration phase; constant power gives a softening one — hence the two-phase feel.',
        visual: 'two-phase-acceleration',
