        complexity: { best: 'the constant torque phase gives nearly constant acceleration', avg: 'two phases must be integrated separately for accurate timing', worst: 'a low corner speed makes most of the acceleration run occur in the declining phase', note: 'Raising the corner speed by gearing improves the acceleration feel but reduces top speed.' },
