        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Drive cycle = a defined speed vs time profile,\nused so consumption figures are comparable.\n\n  URBAN cycle:   low speed, frequent stops\n    drag small; braking energy large\n    -> REGENERATION recovers much of it\n    -> EV consumption LOW\n\n  HIGHWAY cycle: sustained high speed\n    drag dominates (V^2 force, V^3 power)\n    no braking to recover\n    -> EV consumption HIGH\n\nNOTE THE REVERSAL: an EV does BETTER in town,\na petrol car does better on the highway.\n\nAlways ask WHICH CYCLE a quoted range refers to.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.4, pp.112-116.' },
        mistake: 'Students compare quoted range figures between vehicles without checking the cycle. The same vehicle can differ by thirty percent or more between urban and highway cycles, so a comparison across different cycles is meaningless.',
