        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Field weakening (above base speed):\n\n  V is already at maximum -> reduce phi\n\n  omega  proportional to  1/phi     speed RISES\n  T = K*phi*I_a                     torque FALLS\n  P = T*omega  ~ CONSTANT           constant power region\n\nLIMIT: COMMUTATION\n  weaker main flux -> armature reaction is relatively\n  stronger -> the neutral axis shifts -> SPARKING\n  at the brushes worsens\n\n  practical DC machine speed ratio ~ 2\n  (compare: induction ~3-4, SRM higher)\n\nThis modest speed ratio is a principal reason DC drives\nhave been displaced in traction.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, p.146.' },
