        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Combined control strategy:\n\n  BELOW base speed:\n    phi = rated (field current constant)\n    V   varied to control speed\n    -> CONSTANT TORQUE\n\n  AT base speed:  V reaches maximum\n\n  ABOVE base speed:\n    V   = maximum (held)\n    phi varied (reduced) to control speed\n    -> CONSTANT POWER\n\n  phi_required = phi_rated * (omega_base / omega_demand)\n\nThe transition must be SMOOTH or a torque disturbance\nis felt at the crossover.\n\nThis two-region strategy reappears in EVERY drive type\nin Modules 4 and 5.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, p.146.' },
