        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Four-quadrant chopper (H BRIDGE):\n\n  FOUR controlled switches + four anti-parallel diodes\n\n  diagonal pair A -> FORWARD armature voltage\n  diagonal pair B -> REVERSE armature voltage\n  diodes allow current EITHER WAY in each polarity\n\n  -> ALL FOUR QUADRANTS, electronically, no delay\n\nSwitching strategies:\n  BIPOLAR   both diagonals switch; output swings\n            +V to -V; LARGER ripple\n  UNIPOLAR  only one leg switches; output swings\n            +V to 0; ripple roughly HALVED\n\nCost: 4 switches + 4 gate drives, double a two-quadrant\narrangement.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, pp.154-155.' },
