        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Constant V/f control:\n\n  E = K * phi * f      (induced EMF)\n  V ~ E  (neglecting stator impedance)\n\n  -> phi ~ V / f\n\n  HOLD V/f CONSTANT  ->  phi CONSTANT at rated\n                     ->  full TORQUE capability at\n                         every frequency\n\n  400 V / 50 Hz = 8 V per Hz\n  at 30 Hz  ->  apply 240 V\n\nIf V/f is NOT held:\n  V too high for f -> OVER-FLUXING -> saturation,\n                      excessive magnetising current\n  V too low for f  -> UNDER-FLUXING -> reduced torque\n\nThe torque-slip curve TRANSLATES along the speed axis,\nkeeping its shape and peak.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, pp.162-163.' },
