        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Induction drive as a traction solution:\n\n  MERITS\n    no brushes, no magnets, solid cage rotor\n    -> robust, high speed capable, harsh environment OK\n    -> NO rare earth magnet supply exposure\n    wide field weakening (speed ratio ~3-4)\n    -> single gear ratio\n    inverter inherently FOUR-QUADRANT at no extra cost\n\n  LIMITATIONS\n    MAGNETISING CURRENT supplied continuously from\n    the stator -> copper loss even at NO load\n    -> efficiency suffers at LIGHT LOAD,\n       which is where a vehicle actually lives\n    rotor copper loss proportional to slip\n    orientation is PARAMETER SENSITIVE (T_r)\n    usually needs a POSITION SENSOR\n\n-> the PM machine of Module 5 supplies its flux FREE.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, pp.156-186.' },
