        complexity: { best: 'no magnetising current at any load', avg: 'torque directly proportional to current, as in a direct current machine', worst: 'the flux cannot be switched off, which matters at high speed and in a fault', note: 'The magnets produce back electromotive force whenever the rotor turns, whether or not the drive is energised.' },
