        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Back EMF sensing (six-step only):\n\n  in six-step, ONE phase is always OPEN (floating)\n  no current flows in it -> its terminal voltage IS\n  its back EMF\n\n  detect the ZERO CROSSING of that back EMF\n  delay 30 ELECTRICAL DEGREES\n  -> that is the next COMMUTATION instant\n\n  + simple: a voltage measurement and a timer\n  + NO machine model needed\n  - back EMF  proportional to  SPEED\n    -> too small to detect at LOW speed\n    -> ZERO at standstill: method fails completely\n\nStarting: OPEN LOOP sequence until enough speed,\nthen transfer to closed loop.\nUnreliable under load -> suits fans and pumps,\nNOT traction.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, pp.202-203.' },
