        definition:
          'The course forms a single chain. Module 1 established what the vehicle demands, expressed as a tractive effort requirement bounded by tyre adhesion. Module 2 turned that into a torque-speed envelope and showed how the gear ratio and machine speed ratio determine whether one gear suffices. Modules 3 to 5 showed how each machine type produces that envelope and, crucially, how each is controlled to deliver torque on demand. Selecting a traction system means checking a candidate machine and drive against the envelope, the speed ratio, the efficiency over the actual operating region, and the cost and robustness constraints together.',
